From 120818d762e4faabd2e6801c572c7ef5e07161d3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Liew Rui Yan <aethernet65535@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 22 Aug 2026 00:28:26 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 3/4] mm/damon: fix quota could not be set to zero

Problem
=======

When the temporal quota goal tuner determines that the goal has been
achieved (score >= 10000), it sets esz_bp to zero so that the effective
quota becomes zero and the scheme stops applying.  However,
damos_set_effective_quota() unconditionally clamps the quota to
min_region_sz via max(ctx->min_region_sz, esz), preventing the quota
from ever reaching zero.

Solution
========

Skip the min_region_sz clamping when esz is already zero so that the
temporal tuner's intent is respected.

Signed-off-by: Liew Rui Yan <aethernet65535@gmail.com>
---
 mm/damon/core.c | 4 +++-
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/mm/damon/core.c b/mm/damon/core.c
index a09acc2640c0..b1d2c675891c 100644
--- a/mm/damon/core.c
+++ b/mm/damon/core.c
@@ -3124,7 +3124,9 @@ static void damos_set_effective_quota(struct damon_ctx *ctx, struct damos *s)
 		else
 			throughput = PAGE_SIZE * 1024;
 		esz = min(throughput * quota->ms, esz);
-		esz = max(ctx->min_region_sz, esz);
+
+		if (esz)
+			esz = max(ctx->min_region_sz, esz);
 	}
 
 	if (quota->sz && quota->sz < esz)
